    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d244">

                <pb facs="0316" n="250" xml:id="pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/396: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lawton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-23T17:00:00-06:00">January 23, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation in Managua: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 23, 5 p.m. Your January 23, 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">2?</hi>]
                                p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d244-f1"/> Foreign Office has just
                            notified me that President Ubico agrees to recognition on January 25 in
                            manner outlined in my 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">8?</hi>], January 22, 1
                            p.m. to the Department.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to Department and Tegucigalpa.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d244-f1" n="31" xml:id="d244-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph of telegram <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
